OL,3,GNEWSA'Greedy' solicitor used fake
OL,4,Awill-writing invoices to defraud cancer
OL,5,Acharity out of thousands
OL,6,
OL,7,FA solicitor defrauded a cancer charity
OL,8,Fout of thousands of pounds after
OL,9,Fsubmitting fake invoices for work he
OL,10,Fhad not carried out, a court heard.
OL,12,FMichael Fogg, 47, of Cyncoed, Cardiff,
OL,13,Foffered his services to Cancer Research
OL,14,FUK's free will writing scheme, but when
OL,15,Fthe charity contacted people he claimed
OL,16,Fto represent, they said they had not
OL,17,Fused the solicitor.
OL,19,FThe hearing was told the money it lost
OL,20,Fas a result of Fogg's actions could
OL,21,Fhave paid for 48 biopsies.
OL,23,APub: 31-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
